----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: b2-b4, P: b2-b3, R: d1-c1, R: d1-b1, R: d1-a1, R: d1-d2, R: d1-e1, R: f1-e1, K: g1-h1, P: g2-g4, P: g2-g3, P: h2-h4, P: h2-h3]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': '**Evaluation:**  \nFrom the current board, White has two rooks (d1 and f1) and a king on g1, with pawns on b2, g2, h2, and d3.  \nBlack has a queen on d4, pawns on c5, e5, f5, and a rook, bishop, king still on original back rank.  \nOur main threats: Black’s queen is centralized and can cause pressure, but currently not attacking anything critical. Our pawn structure is somewhat loose — pawn on d3 could be a target.\n\nPromising moves:\n\n1. **P: b2-b4** – Gains space, challenges Black’s pawn chain (c5), and opens lines for the rook. Risky if Black can counterattack with ...a5 or if queen moves to b4 pinning something.  \n2. **R: d1-c1** – Defends c2 (though no pawn there now) and eyes the c-file. Not very aggressive.  \n3. **R: d1-d2** – Centralizes the rook and supports d3 pawn, possibly enabling doubling rooks later.  \n4. **R: f1-e1** – Centralizes the other rook, opens f1 for possible king move later.  \n5. **P: g2-g4** – Expands on kingside but weakens king safety; may be premature since king still on g1.\n\nBest practical choice seems **R: d1-d2** because:  \n- Protects the weak pawn on d3.  \n- Connects rooks.  \n- Keeps flexibility for future plans (maybe d2 to d4 or supporting central advance).  \n- Avoids overextending pawns early while improving piece coordination.\n\n**Reason:**  \nIt improves the position without creating new weaknesses, solidifies the center, and prepares to double rooks or contest the d-file.\n\n**Answer: R: d1-d2**'}
