k queen to move, gains time, opens the g2 square for king’s escape if needed, and maintains pawn structure solidity. It’s a standard way to challenge an early queen centralization.  \n\nReason: Forcing the black queen to move disrupts Black's plans and gives White a tempo to complete development (like bringing rooks to better files or moving king to safety). Other moves are either passive or create weaknesses.  \n\nAnswer: P: g2-g3"}
